    id: "f98976953c880b1c7c14",
    cat: "conflitti",
    title: "Israeli attacks kill at least four Palestinians in northern Gaza",
    summary: "Israeli attacks on the occupied Palestinian territory continue despite a 'ceasefire' brokered in October.",
    preview: "Israeli attacks on the Palestinian occupied territory continue despite a ‘ceasefire’ brokered in October. A family of four has been killed in an Israeli airstrike in the northern town of Beit Lahiya, sources told Al Jazeera, as Israel continues to strike the Gaza Strip despite a United States-backed “ceasefire” in effect since October 2025. Israeli warplanes carried out an air attack overnight on Thursday in the vicinity of Kamal Adwan Hospital, killing a Palestinian man, his wife, and their two daughters.",
    body: "Israeli attacks on the Palestinian occupied territory continue despite a ‘ceasefire’ brokered in October.\n\nA family of four has been killed in an Israeli airstrike in the northern town of Beit Lahiya, sources told Al Jazeera, as Israel continues to strike the Gaza Strip despite a United States-backed “ceasefire” in effect since October 2025.\n\nIsraeli warplanes carried out an air attack overnight on Thursday in the vicinity of Kamal Adwan Hospital, killing a Palestinian man, his wife, and their two daughters.\n\nRecommended Stories\n\nlist of 3 items\n\n- list 1 of 3Inside Israel’s prisons, where Ben-Gvir’s cruelty is policy\n\n- list 2 of 3Breathing depends on a cylinder: Gaza faces medical oxygen crisis\n\n- list 3 of 3Israeli strike targets home in Gaza’s al-Shati refugee camp\n\n“The bodies of four members of the Ahmad family were recovered in pieces,” an official at Al-Shifa hospital told the AFP news agency. The children where identifies as aged 12 and eight.\n\nIsraeli helicopters also opened fire overnight in the vicinity of the Jabalia camp, and there were also reports of artillery fire in northern Gaza.\n\nThe Israeli military has been attacking Gaza frequentlyIsrael’s genocidal war on Gaza has killed 73,669 people since October 7, 2023, mostly women and children. According to local authorities, the total number of injuries has reached 174,652.\n\nPalestinian rights advocates have argued that Israel’s ultimate goal is to force Palestinians to leave Gaza. Some far-right Israeli officials have openly called for depopulating the Palestinian enclave.\n\nIsraeli Defence Minister Israel Katz said depopulating Gaza – which some officials euphemistically describe as voluntary “immigration” or “migration” of Palestinians – remains the “only solution”.",
